1
00:04:48,888 --> 00:04:54,888
Some legends will never be forgotten. Some wrongs can never be forgiven.

2
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:43,777
Unforgiven is a western film directed by Clint Eastwood.

3
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:32,666
William Munny is a retired, once-ruthless killer
turned gentle widower and hog farmer.

4
00:19:15,555 --> 00:19:21,555
To help support his two motherless children, he accepts one last
bounty-hunter mission to find the men who brutalized a prostitute.

5
00:24:04,444 --> 00:24:10,444
Joined by his former partner and a cocky
greenhorn, he takes on a corrupt sheriff.

6
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
William Munny, played by Clint Eastwood.

7
00:33:42,222 --> 00:33:48,222
'Little' Bill Daggett, played by Gene Hackman.

8
00:38:31,111 --> 00:38:37,111
Ned Logan, played by Morgan Freeman.

9
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
The Schofield Kid, played by Jaimz Woolvett.

10
00:48:08,888 --> 00:48:14,888
English Bob, played by Richard Harris.

11
00:52:57,777 --> 00:53:03,777
W.W. Beauchamp, played by Saul Rubinek.

12
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Unforgiven is a 1992 American revisionist Western film produced and directed
by Clint Eastwood from a screenplay by David Webb Peoples.

13
01:02:35,555 --> 01:02:41,555
It stars Eastwood as William Munny, an aging outlaw and killer who
takes on one more job years after he turned to farming.

14
01:07:24,444 --> 01:07:30,444
The film co-stars Gene Hackman, Morgan Freeman, and Richard Harris.

15
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
Unforgiven premiered at the Mann Bruin Theater on August 3,
1992 before being released by Warner Bros.

16
01:17:02,222 --> 01:17:08,222
on August 7, 1992.

17
01:21:51,111 --> 01:21:57,111
It grossed over $159 million on a budget of $14.4 million and received widespread critical acclaim, with praise for
the acting (particularly from Eastwood and Hackman), directing, editing, themes, and cinematography.

18
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The film won four Academy Awards: Best Picture, Best Director for Eastwood, Best
Supporting Actor for Hackman, and Best Film Editing for Joel Cox.

19
01:31:28,888 --> 01:31:34,888
Eastwood was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor for his
performance, but lost to Al Pacino for Scent of a Woman.

20
01:36:17,777 --> 01:36:23,777
The film was the third Western to win Best Picture, following
Cimarron (1931) and Dances With Wolves (1990).

21
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
Eastwood dedicated the film (at the end of the credits) to directors and
mentors Sergio Leone and Don Siegel; "Dedicated to Sergio and Don".

22
01:45:55,555 --> 01:46:01,555
In 2004, Unforgiven was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

23
01:50:44,444 --> 01:50:50,444
The film was remade into a 2013 Japanese film, also titled Unforgiven, which stars
Ken Watanabe and changes the setting to the early Meiji era in Japan.

24
01:55:33,333 --> 01:55:39,333
Eastwood has long asserted that the film would be his last traditional Western, concerned that any
future projects would simply rehash previous plotlines or imitate someone else's work.

25
02:00:22,222 --> 02:00:28,222
The film explores themes of prostitute, sheriff,
right and justice, regret, wyoming, usa.

26
02:05:11,111 --> 02:05:17,111
The tone is dark.
